@*
    Blazor Server host page for the planner UI. The desktop app has its own host page
    (APS.DesktopHost/wwwroot/index.html); this is the browser equivalent and renders the same
    APS.UI.Components.Routes root component.

    Kept deliberately close to the desktop host page so the two do not drift: same stylesheet, same
    loading state, same error banner. As there, this file sits outside APS.UI's project tree so
    Tailwind's content scan never sees it - any Tailwind class used here would compile to nothing,
    so the pre-render markup below is styled with plain inline CSS.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>APS Planner</title>
    <base href="/" />
    <script src="_content/APS.UI/theme.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/APS.UI/planning-workbench.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/APS.UI/ui-safety.js"></script>
    <script>window.apsTheme.bootstrap();</script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/APS.UI/tailwind.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
    <style>
        #blazor-error-ui {
            display: none;
            position: fixed;
            left: 0;
            right: 0;
            bottom: 0;
            z-index: 1000;
            padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
            font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.875rem;
            color: #9f1239;
            background: #fff1f2;
            border-top: 1px solid #fecdd3;
        }
        #blazor-error-ui .dismiss {
            float: right;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0; font-family:-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;">
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <div id="blazor-error-ui">
        An unexpected error occurred.
        <a class="dismiss" onclick="document.getElementById('blazor-error-ui').style.display='none'">🗙</a>
    </div>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
